widget.solution:
def volume_by_ticker(trades):
    volume = {}
    for ticker, qty in trades:
        volume[ticker] = volume.get(ticker, 0) + abs(qty)
    return volume

explain.text:
This is the counting idiom with `abs(qty)` in place of 1. Netting would add `qty`; volume ignores the sign. BP traded 800 shares even though the position is only 200.

