def top_and_bottom(returns):
    if len(returns) == 0:
        return None, None
    best = None
    worst = None
    for ticker, r in returns.items():
        if best is None or r > returns[best]:
            best = ticker
        if worst is None or r < returns[worst]:
            worst = ticker
    return best, worst

explain.text:
The early `return None, None` handles the empty book. After that, `best is None` lets the first ticker in, so an all-negative day still has a best. The tuple comes back as one object.

